<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Custom Stickers</p>
      <h1>Custom Sticker Maker</h1>
      <p>
        Create custom stickers from text prompts or portraits. Use simple descriptions for mascots,
        products, pets, characters, objects, and social sticker ideas. Guests get 3 free generations
        with no sign up, and each generation uses 1 credit.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#generator">Make a Custom Sticker</a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel"><h2>Prompt to sticker</h2><p>Describe the subject, style, mood, and useful details. Short prompts usually work best for clean sticker-ready artwork.</p></article>
      <article class="saas-info-panel"><h2>Portrait to sticker</h2><p>Upload a portrait when you want a custom avatar, reaction sticker, or character-like result from a real face.</p></article>
      <article class="saas-info-panel"><h2>Regenerate variations</h2><p>Keep useful prompts in history, then regenerate or make variations when you want a new pose, expression, or color direction.</p></article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Prompt to sticker</h2>
      <p>
        Describe the subject, sticker job, mood, and style. The most reliable pattern is subject
        first, sticker job second, and style last. A specific subject such as a grey tabby cat with
        a green collar usually gives a more useful custom result than a generic cute animal.
      </p>
      <p>
        Custom artwork works best when one prompt has one main subject and one visual anchor. Add a
        clean outline, bold border, simple background, or limited palette before adding extra scene
        details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Portrait to sticker</h2>
      <p>
        Upload a bright, front-facing portrait when you want a custom avatar, reaction sticker, or
        character-like result from a real face. Avoid heavy blur, cropped faces, and very dark light.
      </p>
      <p>
        Upload JPG or PNG files up to 8 MB. Each portrait generation uses 1 credit, and a failed
        generation returns its credit. A saved upload source can be used when retrying a failed item.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Regenerate variations</h2>
      <p>
        Keep useful prompts in history, then regenerate or make variations when you want a new pose,
        expression, or color direction. Reusing the prompt makes a matching set easier to reproduce.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to make a custom sticker</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose one main subject: a pet, mascot, product, character, object, or portrait.</li>
        <li>Add a style such as cute, clean, bold outline, white border, or simple background.</li>
        <li>Describe the mood or action, then generate one sticker or a small prompt batch.</li>
        <li>Use history to retry failed prompts, favorite strong results, and download files.</li>
        <li>Reuse the prompt that worked and change one descriptor to build a matching set.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom stickers for digital use, not for printing</h2>
      <p>
        This page makes downloadable digital artwork for chats, profiles, thumbnails, slides,
        community badges, and designs still in progress. Custom sticker printing is a separate job
        that needs a print vendor, cut path, physical material, and minimum order.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you need vinyl, car decals, bumper stickers, or a printed sheet, use a print service. If
        you need the artwork itself, generate here and download PNG, WebP, or original files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom sticker prompt templates</h2>
      <p>Fill the brackets and keep the rest of the line intact.</p>
      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>[subject] mascot sticker, [emotion], clean white border, simple background</code>
        <code>[product] as a cute character sticker, friendly face, bright colors</code>
        <code>[pet or portrait] avatar sticker, expressive face, crisp outline</code>
        <code>[object] reaction sticker, playful pose, rounded icon style</code>
        <code>[subject] badge sticker, flat colors, centered composition, no text</code>
        <code>[team or community] mascot sticker, bold shapes, two-color palette</code>
        <code>[food or drink] character sticker, glossy highlights, thick outline</code>
        <code>[subject] holiday sticker, festive palette, decorative border</code>
        <code>[character] chibi sticker, oversized head, soft shading, plain background</code>
        <code>[subject] logo-style sticker, sharp edges, high contrast, minimal detail</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom sticker use cases</h2>
      <p>
        Use the custom sticker maker for brand mascots, creator avatars, product reactions,
        classroom icons, community badges, social posts, and design experiments. Keep each prompt
        focused so the sticker subject stays easy to recognize.
      </p>
      <p>
        For personalized sets, reuse the same border, palette, and style language while changing
        only the subject or emotion. That gives pets, team members, or products a coherent collection.
      </p>
      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/ai-sticker-generator"}>AI Sticker Generator</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sticker-maker-online"}>Sticker Maker Online</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/reaction-sticker-maker"}>Reaction Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/cute-sticker-ideas"}>Cute Sticker Ideas</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom sticker FAQ</h2>
      <div class="saas-faq">
        <details open><summary>How do I write a custom sticker prompt?</summary><p>Start with the subject, then add mood, style, and use case. Try cheerful coffee cup mascot, clean white border, cute reaction sticker, simple background.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I make custom sticker batches?</summary><p>Add multiple prompts on separate lines. History groups generated stickers into batches, shows progress, and supports batch download.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What format should I download?</summary><p>PNG is useful for editing and broad compatibility. WebP is smaller for websites and social assets. Original keeps the generated format.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need an account to make a custom sticker?</summary><p>No. Guests can try 3 custom generations with no sign up, and each generation uses 1 credit.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens if a custom generation fails?</summary><p>The credit is returned automatically, and the prompt stays in history so you can retry it without typing it again.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I make a sticker from my own photo?</summary><p>Yes. Upload a JPG or PNG up to 8 MB, such as a pet, product, or portrait, and add a short style prompt.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I use custom stickers commercially?</summary><p>Review the current terms of service before using generated stickers in paid or branded work, since usage terms can change.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
